170
00:23:29.050 --> 00:23:35.340
Curtis Hollis : Well, thinking about the whole process, I think the biggest challenges I usually see are a few things.

171
00:23:35.500 --> 00:23:46.210
Curtis Hollis : First, designing the system and defining each other… each agent's role can be tricky, because it's easy to, like, either make roles too big or too small.

172
00:23:46.230 --> 00:23:58.189
Curtis Hollis : And then agents either overlap or miss tasks, and what helps is searching simple and testing small pieces first, then building up. Second, I think writing system prompts for the agent is sometimes hard.

173
00:23:58.290 --> 00:24:17.929
Curtis Hollis : Because if a prompt isn't clear, the agent might do the wrong thing, and what helps is, iterating and trying variations. And also writing prompts in a way that's easy to understand. And, third, I think debugging is a big challenge too, especially when agents interact, because problems can come from one agent, you know, but affect the whole system.

174
00:24:17.970 --> 00:24:22.530
Curtis Hollis : So what helps is checking each agent individually first, then testing how they work together.

175
00:24:22.670 --> 00:24:35.629
